course: dictionary
lesson: 8991
title: Sixteen and its friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sixteen is the number 16. It comes right after fifteen, so 15 + 1 = 16. Write it as one word: sixteen.
explain: You can build sixteen in two ways: ten and six, or four fours. Four fours is 4 × 4 = 16, which is also called four squared.
explain: Numbers show up in real life too. A pound has 16 ounces, so 16 helps when you weigh things. Sixteen is also an age people celebrate, which is why it is called "sweet sixteen".
fact: «Sixteen» is the number 16, one more than fifteen.
fact: «Sixteen» is ten and six, or four fours.
fact: 4 × 4 = 16, so sixteen is 4 squared.
fact: A pound has 16 ounces.
fact: «Cats sleep about twelve to sixteen hours a day.» Sixteen is the top of that range.
exercise: What number is one more than fifteen? | *Sixteen | Eighteen | Seventeen | Fourteen
exercise: Which sum makes sixteen? | 3 × 3 | 2 × 2 | 5 × 5 | *4 × 4
exercise: «Cats sleep about twelve to sixteen hours a day.» What is the highest number of hours given? | Eight hours | Twelve hours | *Sixteen hours | Twenty hours
test: Sixteen is ten and what? | Seven | Five | *Six | Four
test: Which word is the number 16? | Seventeen | Sixty | *Sixteen | Fifteen
exam: A pack holds 16 ounces, which is one pound. How many ounces are in two pounds? | 48 | 16 | *32 | 24
